      "text": "Two requests with byte-identical bodies, submitted under different policy sets, may execute on different vendors and both succeed.\nIf swapping a vendor requires a code change, a redeploy, or a prompt edit, the principle is violated — no matter what the diagram says.\nThe router is deterministic code and always will be: routing the thing that decides routing would be circular, and a compliance audience\nwill read this assembly line by line. It is under a 70% coverage gate for exactly that reason.",
